@huboard:{"order":397.5}
-->

This follows from #89. The data clerk should be able to use Kujua baseline to:
- Select a person or group of CHWs, type a plain-text unstructured message, and deliver the message via Kujua's already-configured SMS gateway.
- Reply -- using the same or similar interface -- to unstructured text messages (per the definition of 'unstructured' in #89). In this case, the recipient should be auto-populated -- i.e. inferred from the message being replied to.

<!---
@huboard:{"order":37.96875}
-->

possibly add a new role that the 'gateway' user belongs to that is handled specially by kujua.  so if someone has the gateway user/pass they can't login to kujua, or have some limited set of privileges from the web interface.

