We need to include all message data in the export so we know when a message was sent/scheduled/cleared/muted. Might include this in the bulk sms changes since we're modifying the messages structure and could do all testing/releasing in one shot (see #333). 

Example JSON structure, one idea:

```
tasks: [
  {
     "messages": [
        {
          "sent_by": "admin",
          "to": "+525550761785",
          "facility": <embedded facility obj>,
          "message": "foo bar",
          "uuid": "f5daf0c1-61b7-1df5-79bec3aff4a9e750"
        }
      ],
      "state": "sent",
      "timestamp": "2014-02-07T01:11:14.129Z"
      "history":  [
        {
          "state": "scheduled",
          "timestamp": "2014-02-07T01:10:00.000Z"      
        },
        { 
          "state": "pending", 
          "timestamp": "2014-02-07T01:10:24.129Z"
        }
      ]
  }, ...
]
```

Whenever a state for a message changes, we push the previous state into a history list.  Then in the the export you will know when a message was scheduled/muted/sent/cleared, will have columns for each, and you don't have to traverse the revisions of a record to find that info.

