Currently we ship the default translations in the kanso.json and in a file in the kujua-sms package. This sucks because we're duplicating effort and using a custom json format rather than the .properties standard. Include .properties files for each language and import on first run and merge on app update.
### Possible solution

Include the files in api. On each startup update the translations without overwriting user modified translations. To check if the translation has been modified we should store the language default translation, eg:

```
{
  key: 'logout',
  default: 'Log out',
  translations: [
    {
      locale: 'en',
      content: 'Log out',
      default: 'Log out'
    },
    {
      locale: 'ma',
      content: 'putanga',
      default: 'poroporoaki'
    }
  ]
}
```

With this format we can determine that the "en" translation hasn't been modified and can be overwritten by an updated value, but the "ma" translation has so should not be modified.

